[I] The Oil Runtime Compiler

[T] Orc is a library and set of tools for compiling and executing
[T] very simple programs that operate on arrays of data. The "language"
[T] is a generic assembly language that represents many of the features
[T] available in SIMD architectures, including saturated addition and
[T] subtraction, and many arithmetic operations.

[U] http://www.schleef.org/orc/documentation/

[A] David Schleef <ds@schleef.org>
